# The vendor persona of the range: Ridgeline Process Controls' technician
# (DESIGN.md 13). The topology injects this one file, mode 0600, into three nodes:
#   dmz-jump   cm_vendor_sql.py creates the Guacamole account with its TOTP key
#   ews        70-ews-vendor.sh creates the local account the Guacamole session logs in as
#   vendor-ws  cm_vendor_session.py, the technician's scripted session
# so the three always agree.
#
# These are range-only throwaway values, like the WireGuard keys in the scenario:
# they are in the repository on purpose, protect nothing outside the range, and a
# real deployment would generate its own. The cherrymountain app's own credentials
# (cmadmin, Wazuh, InfluxDB, OpenPLC) are generated per experiment and never appear
# here. TOTP is a standard RFC 6238 secret (SHA-1, 6 digits, 30 s), so any
# authenticator works with it; the key is in Base32 as Guacamole stores it.
VENDOR_GUAC_USER=ridgeline-tech
VENDOR_GUAC_PASSWORD=j8DA6yhLbQh3kAEPDMJd
VENDOR_TOTP_SECRET=UNB7G4GBKPWWAEVCDC7ST6SFRPO4DXMC
VENDOR_EWS_USER=ridgeline
VENDOR_EWS_PASSWORD=p4KnhEYChqSfpZ3sExmP
